BDOSXL (probes/disk/bdosxl.asm), 2026-11-17: ($F237) and CSRX after each case, the CF-3300 and zerobas.
Each case starts with a CONOUT CR (column 0) unless fn has bit 7 set ($8x: a CONTINUATION, the count
carries over from the row before). fn: 2 CONOUT, 6 DIRIO, 9 STROUT (one string, its own '$'), $0B CONST.
Bytes: "text", a quoted character, or a decimal code. Raw captures: scratchpad/XL2_stock.out, XL2_ours.out
(rows 0-83 also in XL_stock.out / XL_ours.out, round 1; reproduced exactly on the CF-3300 in round 2).
⚠️ CSRX is CONTAMINATED in rows 35, 40, 42, 43 and 84 (and 85, which continues 84): they begin inside the escape
sequence the row before left unfinished (34: a bare ESC; 39: ESC x; 41, 42, 83: a partial ESC Y), so the leading CR
went to CHPUT's escape. (Row 41 is CLEAN: row 40 completed its ESC x 5. Corrected after the second review.)
The count there is still valid: the BDOS-level CR zeroed it either way.
